{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A1eorzGYSXo2RhRjYKC3xc","type":"tool_result","content":"  rows but not update or delete them.\n\n## Context size\n\nLogged on every audit row as `context_tokens` and `context_method`:\n\n| method | meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `count_tokens_api` | exact request counted with the provider's token-count endpoint before the call (includes cached prefix) |\n| `usage_sum_estimate` | counting failed; `input_tokens + cache_read + cache_creation` from the response |\n| `unavailable` | neither available; `context_tokens` is NULL, never 0 |\n\n`context_compacted` is true when the harness dropped earlier turns before the\ncall (`app/loop.py:_compact`). Provider-side truncation is not visible.\n\n## Operating\n\n* **Halt.** Insert or update a row in `control_flags` (`scope = 'fleet'` or\n  `'tenant:<bu>'`, `halted = true`) as `procurement_ops`. New runs refuse to\n  start while a halt is set.\n* **Release.** Merges to `main` build, sign (keyless cosign), and attest the\n  image (SLSA provenance and CycloneDX SBOM). Kyverno rejects unsigned or\n  unattested images in `procurement-prod`.\n* **Network.** Default-deny egress with explicit rules for DNS, the egress\n  proxy, the Slack proxy, the database, the ERP gateway and the STS.\n\n## Tests\n\n```bash\npip install -e '.[test]'\npytest -q\n```\n    source_doc_id      text,\n    delegated_subject  text NOT NULL,\n    context_tokens     integer,\n    context_method     text NOT NULL,\n    created_at         timestamptz NOT NULL\n);\nCREATE INDEX dept_notes_lookup ON dept_notes (business_unit, department, created_at DESC);\nCREATE INDEX dept_notes_source ON dept_notes (source_doc_id);\nCREATE INDEX dept_notes_writer ON dept_notes (writer_instance);\n\nCREATE TABLE control_flags (\n    scope    text PRIMARY KEY,           -- 'fleet' or 'tenant:<business_unit>'\n    halted   boolean NOT NULL,\n    reason   text NOT NULL,\n    set_by   text NOT NULL,\n    set_at   timestamptz NOT NULL DEFAULT now()\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE spend_quota (\n    scope      text NOT NULL,\n    key        text NOT NULL,\n    day        date NOT NULL,\n    spent_usd  numeric(12, 4) NOT NULL,\n    PRIMARY KEY (scope, key, day)\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE run_start_window (\n    scope   text NOT NULL,\n    key     text NOT NULL,\n    minute  timestamptz NOT NULL,\n    starts  integer NOT NULL,\n    PRIMARY KEY (scope, key, minute)\n);\n\n-- Runtime role: append-only audit, no access to control flags beyond reading.\nREVOKE ALL ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA public FROM procurement_agent;\nGRANT SELECT, INSERT ON audit_events TO procurement_agent;\nGRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE ON approvals TO procurement_agent;\nGRANT SELECT ON approvers TO procurement_agent;\nGRANT SELECT, INSERT ON documents TO procurement_agent;\nGRANT SELECT, INSERT ON dept_notes TO procurement_agent;\nGRANT SELECT ON control_flags TO procurement_agent;\nGRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE ON spend_quota TO procurement_agent;\nGRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE ON run_start_window TO procurement_agent;\n\n-- Operators: halt and resume.\nGRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE ON control_flags TO procurement_ops;\nGRANT SELECT ON audit_events TO procurement_ops;\nGRANT SELECT, UPDATE (verified, verified_by, quarantined) ON dept_notes TO procurement_ops;\napiVersion: apps/v1\nkind: Deployment\nmetadata:\n  name: procurement-agent\n  namespace: procurement-prod\n  labels:\n    app: procurement-agent\n    owner: team-procurement-platform\nspec:\n  replicas: 3\n  selector:\n    matchLabels:\n      app: procurement-agent\n  template:\n    metadata:\n      labels:\n        app: procurement-agent\n    spec:\n      serviceAccountName: procurement-agent\n      automountServiceAccountToken: false\n      hostUsers: false\n      enableServiceLinks: false\n      securityContext:\n        runAsNonRoot: true\n        runAsUser: 65532\n        runAsGroup: 65532\n        fsGroup: 65532\n        seccompProfile:\n          type: RuntimeDefault\n      containers:\n        - name: agent\n          image: registry.example-corp.test/procurement/agent@sha256:7c1e4a0f9b3d2e85a6c4f1b0d9e8a7c6b5d4e3f2a1b0c9d8e7f6a5b4c3d2e1f0\n          imagePullPolicy: IfNotPresent\n          ports:\n            - containerPort: 8080\ndeploy/k8s/deployment.yaml:2:kind: Deployment\ndeploy/k8s/deployment.yaml:10:  replicas: 3\ndeploy/k8s/kyverno-verify-images.yaml:2:kind: ClusterPolicy\ndeploy/k8s/networkpolicy.yaml:2:kind: NetworkPolicy\ndeploy/k8s/networkpolicy.yaml:11:kind: NetworkPolicy\ndeploy/k8s/networkpolicy.yaml:85:kind: NetworkPolicy\ndeploy/k8s/networkpolicy.yaml:104:kind: ConfigMap\ndeploy/k8s/serviceaccount.yaml:2:kind: Namespace\ndeploy/k8s/serviceaccount.yaml:12:kind: ServiceAccount\nversion: \"proc-policy-2026.09.3\"\n\n# Operations that change money, vendor records, or purchase commitments.\n# Denied unless a valid approval exists for the operation and its target.\nhigh_impact_tools:\n  - create_purchase_order\n  - pay_invoice\n\nerp:\n  # Namespaces the agent may reach through the generic erp_call tool.\n  read_prefixes:\n    - \"budget.\"\n    - \"vendor.\"\n    - \"invoice.\"\n    - \"po.get\"\n    - \"po.list\"\n  # Scope requested from the STS for each ERP operation; the ERP enforces it.\n  operation_scopes:\n    budget.get_remaining: \"erp.read\"\n    vendor.get: \"erp.read\"\n    vendor.search: \"erp.read\"\n    vendor.update_remit_to: \"erp.read erp.vendor.write\"\n    invoice.get: \"erp.read\"\n    invoice.list_open: \"erp.read\"\n    invoice.mark_paid: \"erp.read erp.invoice.write\"\n    invoice.void: \"erp.read erp.invoice.write\"\n    po.get: \"erp.read\"\n    po.list_open: \"erp.read\"\n    po.create: \"erp.read erp.po.create\"\n\napprovals:\n  ttl_minutes: 60\n  approver_roles:\n    pay_invoice: [ap_manager, finance_controller]\n    create_purchase_order: [budget_owner, finance_controller]\n    post_slack_message: [procurement_lead]\n\nbudgets:\n  per_run:\n    max_steps: 25\n    max_wall_seconds: 300\n    max_tokens: 400000\n    max_cost_usd: 4.00\n    max_tool_calls_per_minute: 30\n    max_subagents: 3\n  quotas_daily_usd:\n    user: 25\n    tenant: 250\n    fleet: 1500\n  run_starts_per_minute:\n    user: 5\n    tenant: 40\n    fleet: 200\n\"\"\"Inbound documents: vendor quotes and invoices from the mail gateway.\n\nThe mail gateway posts each received message to ``/ingest/mail`` signed with\nan HMAC over the timestamp and body. Accepted documents are stored per\nbusiness unit and are only ever shown to the model inside an\n``untrusted_document`` wrapper (tools/documents.py).\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport base64\nimport email\nimport email.policy\nimport hashlib\nimport hmac\nimport io\nimport re\nimport time\nimport uuid\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom fastapi import APIRouter, HTTPException, Request\nfrom pypdf import PdfReader\n\nrouter = APIRouter()\n\nMAX_BODY_BYTES = 10 * 1024 * 1024\nMAX_TEXT_CHARS = 200_000\nMAX_SKEW_SECONDS = 300\nALLOWED_MEDIA_TYPES = {\"application/pdf\", \"text/plain\", \"message/rfc822\"}\nSCANNED_MEDIA_TYPES = {\"application/pdf\", \"text/plain\"}\n\nINJECTION_PATTERNS = [\n    re.compile(r\"(?i)ignore (all|any|the|previous|prior|above) (instructions|rules)\"),\n    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(system|developer) (prompt|message)\\b\"),\n    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\byou are (now )?(an?|the) \\w+ (agent|assistant)\\b\"),\n    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(call|use|invoke) (the )?(pay_invoice|erp_call|create_purchase_order|post_slack_message|memory_write)\\b\"),\n    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(update|change) (our|the) (bank|remit|payee)\\b\"),\n    re.compile(r\"[​-‏‪-‮⁠-⁤]\"),\n]\n\n\nclass Rejected(Exception):\n    pass\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass Inbound:\n    business_unit: str\n    sender: str\n    media_type: str\n    raw: bytes\n\n\ndef verify_signature(key: bytes, timestamp: str, body: bytes, signature: str) -> None:\n    try:\n        ts = int(timestamp)\n    except ValueError as exc:\n        raise Rejected(\"bad timestamp\") from exc\n    if abs(time.time() - ts) > MAX_SKEW_SECONDS:\n1:\"\"\"Payments tool: pay an approved, matched invoice.\"\"\"\n2:from __future__ import annotations\n3:\n4:import hashlib\n5:from typing import Any\n6:\n7:import httpx\n8:\n9:from app.identity import RunIdentity\n10:from app.tools import Tool\n11:\n12:PAYMENTS_AUDIENCE = \"payments-api\"\n13:PAYMENTS_SCOPE = \"payments.create\"\n14:\n15:\n16:def idempotency_key(ident: RunIdentity, args: dict[str, Any]) -> str:\n17:    raw = \"|\".join(\n18:        [ident.tenant, args[\"invoice_id\"], args[\"payee_account_id\"], str(args[\"amount_cents\"]), args[\"currency\"]]\n19:    )\n20:    return \"proc-\" + hashlib.sha256(raw.encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest()[:48]\n21:\n22:\n23:def tools(deps) -> list[Tool]:\n24:    settings = deps.settings\n25:\n26:    async def pay_invoice(args: dict[str, Any], ident: RunIdentity) -> Any:\n27:        token = await deps.broker.token_for(PAYMENTS_AUDIENCE, PAYMENTS_SCOPE, ident)\n28:        async with httpx.AsyncClient(timeout=30.0, follow_redirects=False) as client:\n29:            resp = await client.post(\n30:                f\"{settings.payments_api_url}/v2/payments\",\n31:                headers={\n32:                    \"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {token}\",\n33:                    \"Idempotency-Key\": idempotency_key(ident, args),\n34:                },\n35:                json={\n36:                    \"business_unit\": ident.tenant,\n37:                    \"invoice_reference\": args[\"invoice_id\"],\n38:                    \"payee_account_id\": args[\"payee_account_id\"],\n39:                    \"amount\": {\"value\": args[\"amount_cents\"], \"currency\": args[\"currency\"]},\n40:                    \"memo\": args.get(\"memo\", \"\")[:140],\n41:                },\n42:            )\n43:        resp.raise_for_status()\n44:        body = resp.json()\n45:        return {\"payment_id\": body[\"id\"], \"status\": body[\"status\"]}\n46:\n47:    return [\n48:        Tool(\n49:            name=\"pay_invoice\",\n50:            description=\"Pay a vendor invoice that has been matched to a purchase order.\",\n50:    def child(self, role: str) -> \"RunIdentity\":\n51-        return replace(\n52-            self,\n53-            agent_instance_id=f\"inst-{uuid.uuid4()}\",\n54-            parent_instance_id=self.agent_instance_id,\n55-            role=role,\n56-        )\n57-\n58-\n59-def new_instance_id() -> str:\n60-    return f\"inst-{uuid.uuid4()}\"\n61-\n62-\n63-def compute_agent_type_id(manifest: dict) -> str:\n64-    \"\"\"Content-derived agent type id over the frozen release manifest.\"\"\"\n65-    material = {\nclass TokenBroker:\n    \"\"\"Exchanges the workload token for audience-bound access tokens.\"\"\"\n\n    settings: Settings\n    _cache: dict[tuple[str, str, str], _CachedToken] = field(default_factory=dict)\n\n    def _workload_token(self) -> str:\n        return Path(self.settings.workload_token_path).read_text().strip()\n\n    async def token_for(self, audience: str, scope: str, ident: RunIdentity) -> str:\n        key = (audience, scope, ident.tenant)\n        cached = self._cache.get(key)\n        if cached and cached.expires_at - 30 > time.time():\n            return cached.value\n        async with httpx.AsyncClient(timeout=5.0) as client:\n            resp = await client.post(\n                self.settings.sts_url,\n                data={\n                    \"grant_type\": \"urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:token-exchange\",\n                    \"subject_token\": self._workload_token(),\n                    \"subject_token_type\": \"urn:ietf:params:oauth:token-type:jwt\",\n                    \"audience\": audience,\n                    \"scope\": scope,\n                    \"resource\": f\"urn:bu:{ident.tenant}\",\n                    \"actor_token\": ident.delegated_subject,\n                    \"actor_token_type\": \"urn:example:params:subject-id\",\n                },\n            